WEBVTT

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:09.000
The ominous sound of the grandfather 
clock before a gruesome murder.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:14.500
The heroic past of a beauty who made 
an outstanding transformation.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:18.420
Mysterious bread placed beside the corpse.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.940
A trap set during the unaccounted-for three minutes!

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:23.000
<b>Train Schedule</b>

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.000
The schedule trick is revealed!

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:28.060
The black shadow approaching 
the beauty in the steam!

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:33.300
"Who would've thought he was the culprit?!"

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:39.040
I-I don't really want to know,
 but I'll ask anyway.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.070
What are you up to now?

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.520
This is it!

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:46.980
<b>Holy Star Festival</b>

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.250
The Holy Star Festival?

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.980
They're known as school 
festivals in your world.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.980
Oh, a school festival?

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.970
Why are you acting like 
it doesn't concern you?

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:53.550
The best situations for men and 
women to pledge their love

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:56.610
are beside bonfires and at school festivals!

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:58.530
Uh, really?

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:01.720
You mustn't waste such a good opportunity!

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:05.820
That's why I suggested this for a 
featured event in the school festival!

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:09.110
<b>Mana Presents!!
Sunday Suspense Theater:
"Mansion of Horror."</b>

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.040
Mana Presents!!

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.670
Sunday Suspense Theater:

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.010
"Mansion of Horror."

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:11.610
How did you come up with that?

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:16.300
Apparently, people end up together when 
they experience the same horror.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:20.220
In other words, horror leads to eroticism!

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.980
I'm going to continue with my script.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.670
All right, good luck with that.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:26.230
A dark inheritance battle!
 Tricks in a locked room!

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:31.780
What the hell is that?!

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.830
Ow!

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.920
Aw, sorry.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:40.280
Are you all right?

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:41.930
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:42.740
Are you okay?

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:46.000
Here, a letter from Collette!

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.760
Please come see my concert!

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.030
Please come see it!

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.340
You've got to be kidding!

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:56.470
You've got to be kidding!

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:58.970
<b>Petting
 Zoo</b>

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:02.470
Wow, everyone's so into it.

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:04.360
Itsuki!

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:05.470
Onii-chan.

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.460
Oh, Mahiru and Yuzuha.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.680
We're going to set up a booth!

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:11.640
Right?

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.810
We have things to prepare,
 so see you later!

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:16.240
Bye-bye, onii-chan.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:20.870
<i>I'm glad Yuzuha seems
 to be in good spirits.</i>

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:25.370
I'm sorry for sending a letter 
to ask you to come.

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:26.890
It's okay.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:28.810
Your letter said you're
 having trouble deciding

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:31.150
what bread to make for the festival.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.120
Yes.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:36.460
The Holy Star Festival is a wonderful 
opportunity to promote our bread.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:38.320
What's that?

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:42.300
A hundred bread recipes that were 
passed down to me by my grandfather!

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:44.160
A hundred?!

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:45.510
There are that many?

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:51.340
Although, the page with the hundredth
 secret recipe was ripped out and lost.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:55.020
It was the secret recipe for my 
grandfather's Happy Bread!

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:57.460
Happy Bread?

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:01.150
My grandfather is very old now,

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:03.240
and he doesn't remember the recipe.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:08.360
I want to revive the Happy Bread 
for the Holy Star Festival!

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:11.120
Then I'm sure our bakery will...

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:15.460
Onii-san, can you please help me out?

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.680
<i>Such a sincere look in her eyes!</i>

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:21.010
Yes, of course.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.510
Thank you so much!

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:25.900
Soon...

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:29.370
Soon, horror and eroticism will become one,

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:33.020
and will reach the ultimate climax!

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.800
Please come see my concert!

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.520
Please come see it!

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.400
You've got to be kidding!

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:40.530
You've got to be kidding!

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:44.860
That lady keeps using the punchline on herself.

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:46.820
What a strange comedy style.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.000
Onii-san, I heard that in your world

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:56.040
you say "I want a piece of her" 
when you describe a cute girl.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:59.300
Well... I guess you might say that.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:02.940
Then, if you think of me as bread,

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:05.300
which part would you want to eat?

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:11.680
The softest part is obviously the tastiest.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:15.310
Which part of me do you think 
is the softest and tastiest?

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:22.860
No, no, no!

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:26.370
Please tell me, onii-san.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.650
W-Well...

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:29.450
Well?

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:30.870
U-Um...

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:35.240
Your ear, I guess...

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:36.710
since I eat bread all y<i>ear</i> around?

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:39.340
Onii-san, you're a surplus of surprises!

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:44.550
That was a pun on surplus and surprise!

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:46.800
I-Is that right?

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:52.310
Well, then, the first Happy Bread
 prototype with your input...

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:57.530
I call it the Happy Ear Bread!

00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:01.070
Now you can have a happy y<i>ear</i>!

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:03.290
By the way, you can also do this...

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:04.820
It got big!

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:08.010
Surplus of surprises?

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:10.240
Please, eat my ear!

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:13.330
O-Okay. I'll have one.

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:18.430
How's my ear?

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:20.540
I-It's tasty.

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:23.360
But this isn't exactly right.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:26.090
Yeah, it's not really your ear.

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:29.970
Would you like this one instead?

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:33.390
I'm just kidding!

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:35.000
What I was trying to say was

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:38.730
that it's not the same as my 
grandfather's Happy Bread.

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:41.440
Sheesh, onii-san. Surplus of surprises!

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:44.990
<i>Wh-What's going on?</i>

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.580
<i>The pure and innocent Collette...</i>

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:50.070
<i>Sometimes feels like she's 
 something else entirely.</i>

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:56.140
Excellent! It is complete!

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:00.090
S-Stop!

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:03.480
Aw, aw! I can't stop whenever I want!

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.840
Prototype #2, Banana Bread!

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:09.100
Why are there eggs attached to the bread?

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:18.350
Bananas are all soft inside 
and maybe a bit hard to eat.

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:22.520
Now that the Mansion of Horror is destroyed,

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:26.360
I'll go with Matryoshka Mana's 
Fortune Telling Mansion!

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:31.370
Tell me, my son, what brings you here today?

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:34.120
My deliveries are too slow.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:37.000
Matryoshka Mana-san, what should I do?

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:42.250
Perhaps your deliveries are too slow 
because you make too many mistakes?

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:45.180
I don't make mistakes!

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:48.760
Delivering to the right address is the 
most basic thing for making deliveries.

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:51.260
Why, then?

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:55.510
My deliveries are slow 
because I run too fast.

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:59.520
They're slow because you're too fast?!

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:01.520
Abalone Bread!

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.560
Why abalone?

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:06.350
It's a girl abalone, just like me!

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:07.980
Does that mean it's female?

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:11.070
You can't tell if an abalone is 
male or female by looking at it.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:13.450
But they say you can find out 
by peeling them like this,

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:16.310
and tell by the color of 
their reproductive glands!

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:20.080
White ones are male, 
and green ones are female!

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.880
By the way, you can only see the 
difference when the abalone liver fattens,

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:27.230
and abalone liver fattens in summer or autumn!

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:28.880
Why did you say that twice?

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:31.630
Onii-san, please try my Abalone Bread!

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:34.360
Please try my Abalone Bread!

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:36.010
You just said that twice, as well.

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:40.040
Aw, I run too fast and can't stop.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:42.020
That's why my deliveries are late.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:45.080
Then you should just deliver less.

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:47.520
Maybe you're trying to deliver 
more than you can handle.

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:48.970
That's not true!

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:51.370
I always split them with my master.

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:55.530
Although it takes me more than twice 
as long to deliver them all.

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:57.780
Then you can just run slowly!

00:07:58.120 --> 00:07:59.840
No!

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:03.500
Letters are filled with the
feelings of the sender!

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:07.290
That's why I want to deliver 
them as quickly as possible!

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:10.480
You're really passionate about your work.

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:13.600
Master taught me everything 
about making deliveries.

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:19.310
Although... Master still doesn't 
consider me very capable,

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:24.310
and at this rate I won't be able 
to become a capable maiden, either.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:27.310
What?! We can't let that happen!

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:29.320
Ark Shell Bread!

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:31.320
Cherry Bread!

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:33.320
Geoduck Bread!

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:35.320
Mango Bread!

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.320
Hamaguri Clam!

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.830
Extra Ripe Durian Bread!

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:42.540
Why alternate between seafood and fruit?

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:45.500
Are they no good?

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:50.000
Huh? Not at all!

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:53.120
When you say happiness, 
you think of clams and fruits!

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:53.760
Right?

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:57.190
Just kidding.

00:08:57.190 --> 00:08:59.070
If you had time to be depressed,

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:01.300
then put on a smile and make bread!

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:04.280
That's what my grandfather taught me.

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:07.310
Onii-san, I remember it now, thanks to you!

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:10.780
My grandfather told me 
how when I was a child.

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:15.320
Grandpa, what are you making today?

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:17.280
I'm making Happy Bread.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:19.530
Happy Bread?

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:25.920
Yes. You have to put in your love 
when making bread, or a child.

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:29.140
When the two are coupled...

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.050
...the legendary bread will be born.

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:35.200
"When the two are coupled..."

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:37.560
What could the two things be?

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:40.680
Onii-san,

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:44.600
please help me couple the two things!

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.090
Please!

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:47.810
O-Okay.

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:51.800
In order to couple the two things,

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:54.790
we tried all possible couplings imaginable.

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:59.320
And, finally, the time has come for 
the two best things to be coupled.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:06.710
Please be slow and gentle, onii-san.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:07.700
Yes.

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:09.430
Ready?

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:11.400
Okay.

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:19.840
Onii-san!

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:30.090
The two are finally coupled.

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:31.770
Its name is Happy...

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:34.170
...Chikuwa Sausage Bread!

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:40.910
<b>Collette's Happy Bread Festival</b>

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.410
<b>Collette's Happy Bread Festival</b>

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:46.410
Collette's Happy Bread Festival, huh?

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:47.630
Yes!

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:51.100
Onii-san, we'll sell lots of 
Happy Chikuwa Sausage Bread,

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:53.660
and get many fans for our bakery!

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:55.850
Yeah, let's work hard together!

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:59.230
Lunch packs?

00:10:59.230 --> 00:11:00.600
Itsuki!

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:02.180
Onii-chan!

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:04.140
Wh-Why?

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:07.430
Why are you setting up beside us?

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:09.820
That's what I said to the committee,

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:13.230
but a weird fortune telling 
shop took our spot.

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:14.970
This was the only spot left.

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:17.790
Also, why are you and Yuzuha selling these?

00:11:17.790 --> 00:11:20.200
I thought it was sold by 
Femiruna's father's company.

00:11:20.590 --> 00:11:23.740
We were given a special mission.

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:26.990
Femiruna's dad asked us to sell these.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:30.710
Apparently, something shocking 
happened to Femiruna recently.

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:34.600
"It doesn't look like she can set up shop 
for the Holy Star Festival this year,

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:36.340
so please take her place."

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:40.840
As for me,

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:45.660
I have gathered a hundred 
Lunch Pack purchase stamps,

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:49.760
so I was appointed Ms. Lunch Pack...

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:51.560
Does this look good on me?

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:52.100
<b>Ms. Lunch
 Pack</b>

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:54.480
Y-Yeah, looks great.

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:56.220
<i>Wh-What should we do?</i>

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:59.110
<i>Who would've thought these two 
would be selling next to Collette?</i>

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:03.630
All right! Let's compete to 
see which team can sell more!

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:05.020
Right, Yuzuha?

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:08.120
We won't lose! Yeah!

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:12.490
I'm relieved to hear that.

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:15.130
Now I can help out Collette 
without feeling guilty.

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:20.380
I'm working hard in the 
Holy Star Festival, too!

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:22.130
Tarua! Hold it right there!

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:30.430
Please deliver a letter for me.

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:31.460
Aw.

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:35.270
We're sold out!

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:36.640
That's great.

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:38.340
Sold out

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:38.270
You've already sold out?

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:43.780
We keep getting more stock from the
factories, so we're still busy!

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:45.400
Incredible...

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:49.770
Femiruna's company is amazing 
because they can mass produce.

00:12:49.770 --> 00:12:51.520
My bakery doesn't stand a chance...

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:52.640
That's not true!

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:55.790
Some things are better made by hand, 
by putting your heart into each and every one.

00:12:57.010 --> 00:12:59.850
Putting my heart into each and every one...

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:02.880
Maybe you're right.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:07.340
Perhaps that's what I'm suited for,
 and the kind of bakery I should strive for.

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:09.260
Thank you so much!

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:13.530
I was able to realize what that really 
matters thanks to you, onii-san.

00:13:13.530 --> 00:13:14.890
I didn't really do anything...

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:17.100
Onii-san, as a sign of my appreciation...

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:19.800
Can you come with me for a while?

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:23.710
Please come see my concert!

00:13:23.710 --> 00:13:26.040
Please come see it!

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:27.530
This way, onii-san!

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:36.790
Onii-san...

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:40.000
I want be like those Happy Breads.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:44.110
I want to be coupled with you, 
and become one.

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:45.200
What?

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:47.660
My grandfather used to say very often that...

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:50.050
"It's easier to do something 
than worry about it."

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:52.390
Does that mean you'll have my child—

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:56.430
No. Will you be my chikuwa?

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:57.980
Yes.

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:12.370
Two will now...

00:14:13.060 --> 00:14:14.740
Become one.

00:14:21.270 --> 00:14:22.270
We sold them!

00:14:22.270 --> 00:14:23.780
We sold them like crazy!

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:27.140
We're sold out, too.

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:28.970
What should we do now?

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:30.260
You two.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:32.460
If there's a shortage of bread,

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:34.970
then let them have panties.

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:39.430
I wonder if Mahiru and the others 
are still selling lunch packs.

00:14:41.150 --> 00:14:42.900
<b>Pack-all-you-want
 panties!</b>

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.250
The mystery of the ancient literature...

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:49.940
Mystery of the ancient literature...

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:53.130
Please come see my concert!

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:55.260
Please come see it!

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:56.660
You've got to be kidding!

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:57.790
You've got to be kidding!

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:00.080
Everyone's working so hard.

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.790
Itsuki! A letter for you!

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:03.130
W-Wait, stop!

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:09.770
Are you all right?

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:11.180
I-I'm all right.

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:13.580
I crash into trees all the time.

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:15.340
Here, this is your letter.

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:16.100
See ya!

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:19.680
<b>Love letter from Canada</b>

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:24.520
<b>Kamako's Noon 

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:24.520
<b>Fortune Telling 
Mansion</b>

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:27.150
I think it's around here...

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:30.300
<b>Delivery Training Mansion</b>

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:29.450
Is that it?

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:39.500
Delivery Training Mansion!

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:42.490
Welcome to "Kamako's Noon!"

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:43.210
Huh?

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:46.940
Now, you can spend the beautiful 
noontime with Kamako and friends,

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:49.630
and become the mail delivery specialist 
you've always dreamed of!

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:52.140
I never dreamed of that. Who's Kamako?

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:56.100
And be approved by the master 
as a capable Visitor!

00:15:56.380 --> 00:15:57.920
Wh-What?

00:15:57.920 --> 00:15:59.100
Letters are feelings!

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:01.350
Run to the goal without 
dropping a single letter!

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:02.360
It doesn't stop! Help!

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:04.330
Hmm... What do you think, Master?

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:05.280
Hm.

00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:06.560
Continue!

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:10.570
No matter the situation, you must accurately 
separate letters by postal code!

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:24.250
What do you think, Master?

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:25.250
Hm!

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:29.740
What on earth was that?

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:31.790
Your path has been cleared!

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:34.360
Itsuki, deliver that letter to Tarua!

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:35.310
To Tarua?

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:36.590
Wait, you're Mana!

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:38.010
Did you realize it just now?

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:43.710
Oh, Tarua?

00:16:43.710 --> 00:16:44.520
What's the matter?

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:49.480
I fell over there and dropped all my letters.

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:53.400
I picked them up in a hurry, 
but I'm still missing one.

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:55.330
Ready, start!

00:16:55.330 --> 00:16:57.320
This is all to save the world!

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:59.020
You're so fast, Narcisstes!

00:16:59.020 --> 00:17:01.410
11, 12, 13...

00:17:01.780 --> 00:17:02.970
13?

00:17:03.970 --> 00:17:05.420
13!

00:17:06.070 --> 00:17:07.900
W-Wait, Narcisstes!

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:09.770
You're fine with just 13?

00:17:09.770 --> 00:17:12.170
It seemed like he could have stuffed more.

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:14.920
I was able to pack 82.

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:17.930
Impressive! Panty packs!

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:20.430
This warmth...

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:22.650
Please come see my concert!

00:17:22.650 --> 00:17:23.430
Please—

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:27.300
No luck.

00:17:28.470 --> 00:17:29.440
Tarua?

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:31.420
I-I lost it...

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:33.710
I lost the precious letter!

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:37.530
You know, it could've been junk mail.

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:42.470
Letters are filled with feelings!

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:46.650
Letters take time to write,

00:17:46.650 --> 00:17:50.840
so there's as many feelings as there are
 minutes spent writing them!

00:17:51.350 --> 00:17:54.920
And I lost it!

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:55.850
I...

00:17:57.590 --> 00:18:00.540
Tarua, let's get out of this mud pit first.

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:02.120
Your shoes are covered in mud.

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:04.040
But... But...

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:06.140
There's nothing you can do if it's lost.

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:08.440
I'm sure they'll forgive 
you when you apologize.

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:09.980
Aw, aw...

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:11.720
Come on, get out of the mud pit.

00:18:11.720 --> 00:18:13.960
Let's dry our clothes by that tree—

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:18.480
Tarua, is there something 
caught on that tree branch?

00:18:20.770 --> 00:18:22.700
I-It's the letter!

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:25.700
Here, Tarua.

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:27.450
I'm so relieved!

00:18:27.450 --> 00:18:29.390
You found it for me, Itsuki!

00:18:29.390 --> 00:18:30.570
Thank you...

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:32.000
Thank you, Itsuki!

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.990
Tarua, I'm covered in mud! You'll get dirty!

00:18:34.990 --> 00:18:38.470
It's fine! I'm covered in mud, too!

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:41.080
What's that?

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:41.970
Oh, right.

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:43.970
I was told to deliver this to you.

00:18:46.340 --> 00:18:48.890
This wax seal is my master's.

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:53.990
What did he write?

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:59.150
It's very good news for you, too.

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:00.860
For me?

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:04.570
Oh, sorry, I have to deliver 
the rest of the letters.

00:19:04.570 --> 00:19:06.600
I'll go deliver them at full speed!

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:07.980
Thank you so much!

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:09.100
Wait.

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:09.780
Huh?

00:19:10.850 --> 00:19:13.210
Two of us can get this done faster!

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:14.540
Yeah!

00:19:14.890 --> 00:19:17.900
Thanks to you, there's only one left.

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:20.120
So what's the address?

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:21.370
Right here.

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:22.350
Right here?

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:23.460
Here.

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:25.560
For me?

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:27.490
from Tarua

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:29.900
I wrote it in a rush earlier.

00:19:29.900 --> 00:19:33.320
I would only deliver a letter 
without a stamp for you.

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:34.510
Can I read it now?

00:19:34.510 --> 00:19:36.730
No! You're embarrassing me!

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:41.450
But if this letter is your feelings, 
then I want to see it right away.

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:42.490
May I?

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:46.280
Fine. Please read it while I'm turned around.

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:47.330
Okay.

00:19:48.740 --> 00:19:51.330
Thank you for searching 
for the lost letter earlier.

00:19:51.970 --> 00:19:54.460
Thank you for helping me 
with the delivery, too.

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:57.960
I'm starting to like you a lot!

00:19:58.440 --> 00:19:59.710
Did you finish reading it?

00:19:59.710 --> 00:20:02.970
Uh, please stay like that for a while.

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:06.280
Done yet?

00:20:06.280 --> 00:20:07.970
Okay. Look this way.

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:11.230
<b>To Tarua</b>

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:10.870
Please deliver this for me.

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:14.480
It's for me.

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:17.980
I've never sent a letter without a stamp 
to anyone but you before, too, Tarua.

00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:20.600
Aw! Can I read it now?

00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:21.430
Yeah.

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:26.490
It says, "I want you to have my child."

00:20:26.960 --> 00:20:28.010
Will you?

00:20:29.970 --> 00:20:34.490
I heard in the classroom that it would 
make you happy if I kiss your cheek.

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:40.800
I prefer pats over kisses.

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:42.620
I see. Then...

00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:47.310
Actually, in that letter, my Master wrote

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:50.090
"I'm not worried about 
you being with Itsuki."

00:20:50.090 --> 00:20:53.270
"Perform your duty as a maiden."

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:57.900
So, I'll have your child!

00:20:59.380 --> 00:21:00.500
Tarua...

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:06.780
Are you nervous?

00:21:10.630 --> 00:21:13.790
I'm calm now. I'm ready, Itsuki.

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:22.710
Now we've cleared the 9th and the 10th!

00:21:22.710 --> 00:21:25.310
All according to my plan!

00:21:25.310 --> 00:21:28.390
The day when all the Impurities are 
cleansed is not too far away!

00:21:29.860 --> 00:21:32.140
Yay!

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:39.900
95, 96, 97,

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:42.550
98, 99!

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:44.990
Pack-all-you-want panties!

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:47.530
I tried it too, and I packed so many!

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:48.750
Surplus of surprises!

00:21:48.750 --> 00:21:51.820
Looks like I won't have to 
buy panties anytime soon.

00:21:51.820 --> 00:21:53.880
Get good panties and socks.

00:21:53.880 --> 00:21:55.880
That's one of my grandfather's 
teachings, too!

00:21:57.670 --> 00:21:59.920
<b>Please Be My Chikuwa!</b>

00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:39.930
My Child, Welcome!

00:23:37.390 --> 00:23:39.180
Meatballs.
